1. Charter Purpose

This charter translates the approved Stage 1 product concept into an actionable and controlled MVP plan.

It defines:

what the first version of TENTORA must prove;

which users and sectors it will serve;

what functionality is included and excluded;

the required deliverables and acceptance criteria;

how success will be measured;

which assumptions, constraints, and risks must be managed; and

what the team must approve before technical design begins.

This charter controls MVP scope. Features outside it require an explicit change decision rather than being added informally during design or development.

2. Project Purpose

TENTORA is an AI-powered, curated creative-solutions platform that gives project owners two connected ways to obtain creative work:

Design Now: Select a Ready Interactive Design, customize it within creator-defined boundaries, then save, purchase, or export a usable result.

Work With a Creative: Define visual taste, receive up to six compatible creative, studio, or team recommendations, select the preferred option, and organize the project through delivery.

The MVP is intended to test whether this model can:

reduce unnecessary search;

make creative services easier to understand;

simplify visual decisions;

preserve consistency across multiple services;

produce relevant and explainable recommendations;

protect creator rights; and

connect self-service design with professional creative execution.

3. Product Definition

TENTORA begins with a project sector and relevant service, not an open directory of creative profiles or a long technical questionnaire.

flowchart LR
    A[Select Sector] --> B[Explore or Select Service]
    B --> C{Choose a path}
    C --> D[Design Now]
    C --> E[Work With a Creative]

The two paths address different levels of urgency and complexity while remaining connected. A user may customize a Ready Design first and later transfer the saved work to a suitable creative for professional development.

TENTORA is not:

a conventional freelance marketplace;

a generic template library;

a fully autonomous AI design generator;

a simple portfolio directory; or

a replacement for artists and designers.

It is a structured system connecting Ready Interactive Designs, controlled AI assistance, visual taste, curated creative matching, and project delivery.

