8. Functional Requirements

The keywords must, should, and may indicate required, recommended, and optional behavior respectively.

8.1 Sector and service discovery

FR-01: The system must display the five approved sectors.

FR-02: The system must display relevant services and curated examples after sector selection.

FR-03: The system must provide clear access to both product paths from a relevant service.

8.2 Design Now

FR-04: The system must display Ready Designs relevant to the selected sector and service.

FR-05: The system must identify the original creator of every Ready Design.

FR-06: The editor must load only properties allowed by the design definition.

FR-07: The user must be able to preview changes before saving or exporting.

FR-08: AI-assisted actions must preserve approved design rules.

FR-09: A saved session must retain the selected design, values, client content, and uploaded assets.

FR-10: Every pilot design must support at least one validated output type.

8.3 Project needs and taste

FR-11: A client must be able to add one or multiple services to My Project Needs.

FR-12: Each project must have one image-based Taste Discovery exercise.

FR-13: The system must produce and store one Main Taste Profile.

FR-14: The Main Taste Profile must apply to selected services by default.

FR-15: A client may create an optional service direction through a shorter refinement.

FR-16: The system must not require the full taste exercise to be repeated within the same project.

8.4 Creative DNA and matching

FR-17: The system must store structured Creative DNA for every approved creative.

FR-18: Creative DNA must include services, sector relevance, visual attributes, and portfolio evidence.

FR-19: Matching must consider sector, services, Main Taste Profile, optional service directions, and Creative DNA.

FR-20: Matching must return no more than six recommendation options.

FR-21: An option may represent one creative, multidisciplinary studio, or compatible team.

FR-22: Every result must explain its major recommendation reasons.

8.5 Portfolio and selection

FR-23: Clients must be able to inspect relevant portfolio work and services.

FR-24: Clients should be able to save, compare, and select an option.

FR-25: Project services and taste context must persist during selection.

8.6 Project workspace

FR-26: The system must create a workspace when a professional project begins.

FR-27: The workspace must store the project summary, services, taste direction, references, files, feedback, milestones, responsibilities, and delivery state.

FR-28: Client and creative must be able to exchange project messages and files.

8.7 Design-to-Creative handoff

FR-29: A Design Now user must be able to choose Continue With a Creative.

FR-30: The system must transfer the design, customizations, content, and assets into the project context.

FR-31: The handoff must not request information already stored in the design session.

8.8 Authentication

FR-32: Initial sector, service, work, and Ready Design exploration must not require login.

FR-33: Authentication must be required when persistent identity, ownership, purchase, export, or project collaboration requires it.

