14. Assumptions and Constraints

14.1 Assumptions

A permissioned portfolio set can be obtained and consistently classified.

Ready Design contributors will provide explicit customization and licensing permissions.

A controlled two-dimensional editor can validate the concept before motion or 3D tools.

Weighted tag matching can validate the early recommendation experience.

Users value both immediate self-service output and access to human creative expertise.

14.2 Constraints

Development time and team capacity are limited.

Editor features and AI actions must remain controlled.

Matching quality depends on portfolio and taste-data quality.

The MVP will not have enough behavioral data for a mature learned recommendation model.

Copyright, consent, licensing, privacy, and data requirements constrain permitted use.

